## Requirement
# REQ-17 Round discounts to the nearest cent

Checkout and Order Import round discounts to the nearest cent, with
half-cents rounded up.

- With a 105-cent order and a 10% discount, the discount is 11 cents and the
  total is 94 cents.
- Behaviour to preserve: at zero discount the total stays 105 cents.

Affected workflows: Checkout, Order Import.


## Author's PR brief (claims by the author; not yet verified)
Author: Coding agent (authoring pass)
Why: REQ-17 says discounts round to the nearest cent, with half-cents rounded up. The shared pricing function rounded the discount down.
Before: A 105-cent order at 10% gets a 10-cent discount. Total 95 cents.
After: A 105-cent order at 10% gets an 11-cent discount. Total 94 cents.
Behaviour to preserve: At zero discount the total stays 105 cents.
Approach: In applyDiscount(), add 50 before the integer division by 100 so half-cents round up. Whole-cent integer maths only.
Alternatives considered: None recorded
Rollback: Revert the PR commits. No data migration.
Open gaps stated by author: Negative or over-100 percents are rejected as before; no new test added for them.
Claims:
- applyDiscount() now rounds the discount to the nearest cent, half-cents up.
- Checkout totals 94 cents for a 105-cent order at 10%.
- Order Import totals 94 cents for a 105-cent order at 10%.
- At zero discount the Checkout total stays 105 cents.
- At zero discount the Order Import total stays 105 cents.
- All tests pass.
- applyDiscount() has no callers other than Checkout and Order Import.

